IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cards-domain`
IMPORT `earn-kernel`
IMPORT fixtures

§ `Terms and Conditions Governing UOB PRVI Miles Card`

-- ===========================================================================
-- DOCUMENT. uob-prvi-miles-tnc: "Terms and Conditions Governing UOB PRVI
-- Miles Card", "Updated 31 July 2026 (Ver 3.4)" (United Overseas Bank Limited),
-- cl.1-6. It governs the PRVI Miles American Express, World Mastercard and
-- Visa. 1 UNI$ = 2 miles (cl.1(i): "current conversion rate: UNI$1 = 2 miles";
-- "A conversion fee will apply for each conversion").
--
-- WHAT THE TEXT SAYS.
--   cl.1(vii)  UNI$3.5 per S$5 spend in Singapore = 1.4 miles per S$1.
--   cl.1(viii) The same UNI$3.5 per S$5 on SimplyGo (ABT) bus and train fares
--              (World Mastercard: posted every 5 days or at S$15 of rides;
--              Amex and Visa: accumulated per calendar month, awarded on the
--              7th of the next). Timing only; the rate is the local rate.
--   cl.1(ix)   UNI$6 per S$5 overseas = 2.4 mpd. "card transactions made
--              overseas but effected/charged in Singapore dollars and/or online
--              transactions effected in foreign currencies with merchants whose
--              payment gateway sits in Singapore will not be treated as
--              overseas transactions and will earn UNI$3.5 per S$5 spend."
--   cl.1(x)    "Regional": UNI$7.5 per S$5 = 3 mpd, for transactions "effected
--              overseas in Indonesian Rupiah (IDR), Malaysian Ringgit (MYR),
--              Thai Baht (THB) and Vietnamese Dong (VMD) with merchants whose
--              payment gateway is in Indonesia, Malaysia, Thailand and Vietnam
--              respectively". The same Singapore-dollar and Singapore-gateway
--              carve-outs apply. ("VMD" is the document's spelling of the dong.)
--   cl.1(xi)   American Express only: UNI$10,000 (20,000 miles) for spending
--              S$50,000 by the end of the membership year; S$80,000 for cards
--              approved on or after 1 August 2026, and for earlier cards from the
--              first statement date of the membership year on or after 1 October
--              2026. cl.1(xii): annual fee waiver at S$50,000.
--   cl.2       Travel Partner Perks: Expedia (booking period 1 April 2026 to 31
--              March 2027) and Agoda (booking period 15 January 2025 to 15
--              August 2027), at higher rates.
--   cl.4       American Express only: 5,000 bonus miles (UNI$2,500) per quarter
--              from 1 July 2026 with at least S$8,000 of overseas spend, in
--              person (card-not-present excluded).
--   cl.1(ii)   What earns nothing: by kind, by listed MCC, by bill payment
--              and top-up, by descriptor, by SPC (except Amex) and Shell
--              service stations.
--   cl.1(iv)   "UNI$ shall be calculated based on the transaction amount of each
--              transaction and rounded down to the nearest UNI$."
--
-- THE FORK F-uob-per-five. "UNI$3.5 per S$5 spend": complete S$5 blocks
-- (S$4.99 earns nothing) or pro rata? Whole blocks is the narrower reading. The module
-- floors on blocks and ceilings on pro rata (earn-kernel.l4).
--
-- THE FORK F-prvi-package. Expedia's table gives UNI$20 per S$5 for hotels
-- and other products and UNI$7.5 for flights, and cl.2(i)(B)(c) makes a
-- package booking (flight + hotel in one transaction) eligible without saying
-- which rate. Floor 7.5, ceiling 20, open reading named.
--
-- THE FORK F-bill-payments (shared with Citi, yuu, PAssion). cl.1(ii)(b)
-- excludes "all transactions in relation to or in connection with bill
-- payment". A bill paid directly to the biller on the card is arguably "in
-- connection with" one. Floor 0, ceiling the full earn.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `cl.1(ii) -- what earns nothing`

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the PRVI excluded category codes` MEANS
    LIST 4829, 4900, 5199, 5960, 5965, 5993, 6012, 6050, 6051, 6211, 6300, 6513, 6529, 6530, 6534,
         6540, 7349, 7511, 7523, 7995, 8062, 8211, 8220, 8241, 8244, 8249, 8299, 8398, 8651, 8661,
         8699, 8999, 9211, 9222, 9223, 9311, 9399, 9402, 9405

GIVEN k IS A `Charge kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`PRVI cl.1(ii) excludes the kind` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `Retail purchase`                                   THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Bill payment`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Top-up of a prepaid card or stored-value account`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Payment of funds to a payment service provider`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Instalment plan charge`                            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `My Preferred Payment Plan charge`                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Cash advance`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Balance transfer or funds transfer`                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Fee, interest or finance charge`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Pre-authorisation`                                 THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Payment through UOB Payment Facility`              THEN FALSE
    WHEN `NETS or NETS-related transaction`                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SmartPay or personal loan`                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Transit-related transaction`                       THEN FALSE

-- cl.1(ii)(c): the thirty-two listed transaction descriptions, folded to
-- counterparties. The asterisk "signifies that any number of characters may
-- follow", so TRANSIT* reaches Transit Link and AMAZE* reaches every Amaze line.
GIVEN d IS A Descriptor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`PRVI cl.1(ii)(c) lists the description` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `AXS`                                                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Amaze`                                                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Amaze with a transit or payment counterparty`         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `EZ-Link`                                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `FlashPay`                                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `NETS VCashCard`                                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `TRANSIT`                                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Transit Link`                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Razerpay`                                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SingPost-SAM`                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `iPayMy`                                               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SmoovPay`                                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `PayPal Bizconsulta or Capitalroya or Oandaasiapa`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Moneybookers`                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Skrill`                                               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `OANDA`                                                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Saxo`                                                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `IG Markets`                                           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SkyFX`                                                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Banc de Binary`                                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `RWS-Levy`                                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `NORWDS`                                               THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                                                        FALSE

-- cl.1(ii)(d): SPC Service Stations "(except for UOB PRVI Miles American
-- Express)" and Shell Service Stations.
GIVEN c IS A Card, seller IS A Merchant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`PRVI cl.1(ii)(d) excludes the merchant` c seller MEANS
    seller EQUALS `Shell service station`
    OR (seller EQUALS `SPC service station` AND NOT (c EQUALS `UOB PRVI Miles American Express`))

GIVEN c IS A Card, p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`PRVI excludes the purchase` c p MEANS
    `PRVI cl.1(ii) excludes the kind` (p's `charge kind`)
    OR `the code is among` p `the PRVI excluded category codes`
    OR `PRVI cl.1(ii)(c) lists the description` (p's descriptor)
    OR `PRVI cl.1(ii)(d) excludes the merchant` c (p's merchant)
    OR p's `later reversed`


§§ `cl.1(vii)-(x) -- the three rates, UNI$ per S$5`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`PRVI UNI$ per S$5 in Singapore` MEANS 3.5

GIVETH A NUMBER
`PRVI UNI$ per S$5 overseas` MEANS 6

GIVETH A NUMBER
`PRVI UNI$ per S$5 in a Regional currency` MEANS 7.5

-- UNI$1 = 2 miles (cl.1(i)).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`miles per UNI$` MEANS 2

-- cl.1(x): the four Regional currencies and the gateway country each needs.
GIVEN cur IS A Currency, gate IS A Gateway
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the currency and gateway are a Regional pair` cur gate MEANS
    (cur EQUALS `Indonesian rupiah` AND gate EQUALS `A gateway in Indonesia`)
    OR (cur EQUALS `Malaysian ringgit` AND gate EQUALS `A gateway in Malaysia`)
    OR (cur EQUALS `Thai baht` AND gate EQUALS `A gateway in Thailand`)
    OR (cur EQUALS `Vietnamese dong` AND gate EQUALS `A gateway in Vietnam`)

-- cl.1(ix): overseas = a foreign currency AND a gateway outside Singapore.
GIVEN cur IS A Currency, gate IS A Gateway
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the currency and gateway are overseas` cur gate MEANS
    NOT (cur EQUALS `Singapore dollars`)
    AND NOT (gate EQUALS `A gateway in Singapore`)
    AND NOT (gate EQUALS `Gateway not known`)

-- The rate on a purchase whose gateway is settled (known, or stood in).
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the PRVI rate per S$5 on` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the currency and gateway are a Regional pair` (p's currency) (p's gateway)
            THEN `PRVI UNI$ per S$5 in a Regional currency`
        IF `the currency and gateway are overseas` (p's currency) (p's gateway)
            THEN `PRVI UNI$ per S$5 overseas`
        OTHERWISE `PRVI UNI$ per S$5 in Singapore`

-- The gateway that would pay most for a currency, for the best-case evaluation.
GIVEN cur IS A Currency
GIVETH A Gateway
`the gateway that pays most for` cur MEANS
    CONSIDER cur
    WHEN `Indonesian rupiah`        THEN `A gateway in Indonesia`
    WHEN `Malaysian ringgit`        THEN `A gateway in Malaysia`
    WHEN `Thai baht`                THEN `A gateway in Thailand`
    WHEN `Vietnamese dong`          THEN `A gateway in Vietnam`
    WHEN `Another foreign currency` THEN `A gateway in another country`
    WHEN `Singapore dollars`        THEN `A gateway in Singapore`


§§ `cl.2 -- the Travel Partner Perks`

-- Expedia (cl.2(i)(A)): booking period 1 April 2026 to 31 March 2027, both
-- inclusive; UNI$20 per S$5 (base 3.5 + bonus 16.5) for an Eligible Hotel and
-- for "any other eligible products/services: Activities, Cars"; UNI$7.5 (base
-- 3.5 + bonus 4) for an Eligible Flight on an Expedia Participating Airline.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is inside the Expedia booking period` p MEANS
    p's `date charged` AT LEAST Date 1 4 2026 AND p's `date charged` AT MOST Date 31 3 2027
    AND p's `date posted` AT LEAST Date 1 4 2026 AND p's `date posted` AT MOST Date 31 3 2027

-- Agoda (cl.2(ii)(A)): booking period 15 January 2025 to 15 August 2027; local
-- spend UNI$17.5 per S$5 (base 3.5 + bonus 14); overseas spend in other
-- foreign currencies UNI$20 (base 6 + bonus 14). Accommodation bookings for
-- Japan are not Agoda Qualifying Transactions (cl.2(ii)(B)(a)); neither is a
-- pay-later room.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is inside the Agoda booking period` p MEANS
    p's `date charged` AT LEAST Date 15 1 2025 AND p's `date charged` AT MOST Date 15 8 2027

-- The rate on a portal purchase, or 0 if the purchase is not a perk purchase.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the PRVI portal rate per S$5 on` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF p's merchant EQUALS `Expedia PRVI site` AND `the purchase is inside the Expedia booking period` p AND p's item EQUALS `An Expedia prepaid hotel booking`
            THEN 20
        IF p's merchant EQUALS `Expedia PRVI site` AND `the purchase is inside the Expedia booking period` p AND p's item EQUALS `An Expedia flight booking on a participating airline`
            THEN 7.5
        IF p's merchant EQUALS `Expedia PRVI site` AND `the purchase is inside the Expedia booking period` p AND p's item EQUALS `An Expedia package booking`
            THEN 7.5
        IF p's merchant EQUALS `Agoda PRVI site` AND `the purchase is inside the Agoda booking period` p AND p's item EQUALS `An Agoda prepaid hotel booking` AND p's currency EQUALS `Singapore dollars`
            THEN 17.5
        IF p's merchant EQUALS `Agoda PRVI site` AND `the purchase is inside the Agoda booking period` p AND p's item EQUALS `An Agoda prepaid hotel booking`
            THEN 20
        OTHERWISE 0

-- The package's other reading (fork F-prvi-package): the hotel rate.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is an Expedia package in the booking period` p MEANS
    p's merchant EQUALS `Expedia PRVI site`
    AND `the purchase is inside the Expedia booking period` p
    AND p's item EQUALS `An Expedia package booking`


§§ `The answer for one purchase`

GIVEN perFive IS A NUMBER, amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF Condition
`PRVI rounding conditions at` perFive amount MEANS
    IF `UNI$ by whole S$5 blocks` amount perFive EQUALS `UNI$ pro rata` amount perFive
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`

-- The answer when the facts are settled: gateway known, code irrelevant (PRVI
-- has no category).
GIVEN c IS A Card, p IS A Purchase, perFive IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`PRVI answer at a rate of` c p perFive MEANS
    `an answer for` c `in` `UNI$` `of` (`UNI$ by whole S$5 blocks` (p's `amount in SGD`) perFive) `to` (`UNI$ pro rata` (p's `amount in SGD`) perFive) `wanting` 0 `at` (JUST `miles per UNI$`) `excluded` FALSE `drawing on` `No pot` `depending on` (`PRVI rounding conditions at` perFive (p's `amount in SGD`)) `per` "UOB PRVI Miles T&C cl.1(iv), 1(vii)-(x)"

-- Settled: choose the rate by the facts.
GIVEN c IS A Card, p IS A Purchase
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`PRVI answer when the gateway is settled` c p MEANS
    IF `PRVI excludes the purchase` c p
    THEN `nothing is earned on` c `in` `UNI$` `per` "UOB PRVI Miles T&C cl.1(ii)"
    ELSE IF `the PRVI portal rate per S$5 on` p GREATER THAN 0
         THEN `PRVI answer at a rate of` c p (`the PRVI portal rate per S$5 on` p)
         ELSE `PRVI answer at a rate of` c p (`the PRVI rate per S$5 on` p)

GIVEN c IS A Card, p IS A Purchase
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`PRVI answer at the worst gateway` c p MEANS
    `PRVI answer when the gateway is settled` c (`rerouted purchase` p `A gateway in Singapore`)

GIVEN c IS A Card, p IS A Purchase
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`PRVI answer at the best gateway` c p MEANS
    `PRVI answer when the gateway is settled` c (`rerouted purchase` p (`the gateway that pays most for` (p's currency)))

GIVEN c IS A Card
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`PRVI earns nothing under the open reading` c MEANS
    `nothing is earned on` c `in` `UNI$` `per` "UOB PRVI Miles T&C cl.1(ii)(b) (open reading)"

GIVEN c IS A Card, p IS A Purchase
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`PRVI answer for an Expedia package` c p MEANS
    `bracketed from` (`PRVI answer at a rate of` c p 7.5) `to` (`PRVI answer at a rate of` c p 20) `adding` (LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)

GIVEN c IS A Card, p IS A Purchase
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` c p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the purchase is an Expedia package in the booking period` p AND NOT (`PRVI excludes the purchase` c p)
            THEN `PRVI answer for an Expedia package` c p
        IF p's `charge kind` EQUALS `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`
            THEN `bracketed from` (`PRVI earns nothing under the open reading` c) `to` (`PRVI answer when the gateway is settled` c p) `adding` (LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)
        IF p's gateway EQUALS `Gateway not known` AND NOT (p's currency EQUALS `Singapore dollars`)
            THEN `bracketed from` (`PRVI answer at the worst gateway` c p) `to` (`PRVI answer at the best gateway` c p) `adding` (LIST `The merchant's payment gateway is not known`)
        OTHERWISE `PRVI answer when the gateway is settled` c p


§§ `cl.1(xi), cl.1(xii), cl.4 -- the American Express bonuses`

-- cl.1(xi): the S$ spend threshold for the UNI$10,000 loyalty bonus. A card
-- approved on or after 1 August 2026 faces S$80,000. A card approved before
-- that faces S$80,000 only from the first statement date of the membership year
-- on or after 1 October 2026; before that, S$50,000.
GIVEN approvedOn IS A DATE, membershipYearStartsOn IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the PRVI Amex loyalty bonus threshold in S$ for a card approved on` approvedOn `in the membership year starting` membershipYearStartsOn MEANS
    IF approvedOn AT LEAST Date 1 8 2026
    THEN 80000
    ELSE IF membershipYearStartsOn AT LEAST Date 1 10 2026
         THEN 80000
         ELSE 50000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the PRVI Amex loyalty bonus in UNI$` MEANS 10000

GIVEN spend IS A NUMBER, threshold IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the PRVI Amex loyalty UNI$ for spend of` spend `against` threshold MEANS
    IF spend AT LEAST threshold THEN `the PRVI Amex loyalty bonus in UNI$` ELSE 0

-- cl.1(xii): annual fee waiver on S$50,000 of spend on the anniversary date.
GIVEN spend IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PRVI Amex annual fee is waived on spend of` spend MEANS
    spend AT LEAST 50000

-- cl.4: 5,000 bonus miles (UNI$2,500) in a quarter with at least S$8,000 of
-- overseas in-person spend, from 1 July 2026, Amex only.
GIVEN overseasInPersonSpend IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the PRVI Amex quarterly bonus UNI$ for overseas in-person spend of` overseasInPersonSpend MEANS
    IF overseasInPersonSpend AT LEAST 8000 THEN 2500 ELSE 0


§§ `Illustrations -- built from cl.1(vii)-(x) and cl.1(iv)`

`PRVI Visa` MEANS `UOB PRVI Miles Visa`
`PRVI Amex` MEANS `UOB PRVI Miles American Express`

`S$100 local` MEANS `the base purchase`
`S$100 in Singapore dollars overseas` MEANS `purchase at location` `the base purchase` `A store outside Singapore`
`S$100 in US dollars through a gateway overseas` MEANS `purchase described as` (`rerouted purchase` (`purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Another foreign currency`) `A gateway in another country`) `Another description`
`S$100 in US dollars through a Singapore gateway` MEANS `rerouted purchase` (`purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Another foreign currency`) `A gateway in Singapore`
`S$100 in US dollars, gateway not known` MEANS `rerouted purchase` (`purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Another foreign currency`) `Gateway not known`
`S$100 in ringgit through a Malaysian gateway` MEANS `rerouted purchase` (`purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Malaysian ringgit`) `A gateway in Malaysia`
`S$100 in ringgit through a Thai gateway` MEANS `rerouted purchase` (`purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Malaysian ringgit`) `A gateway in Thailand`
`S$100 in ringgit through a Singapore gateway` MEANS `rerouted purchase` (`purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Malaysian ringgit`) `A gateway in Singapore`
`S$100 in ringgit, gateway not known` MEANS `rerouted purchase` (`purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Malaysian ringgit`) `Gateway not known`
`S$100 in rupiah through an Indonesian gateway` MEANS `rerouted purchase` (`purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Indonesian rupiah`) `A gateway in Indonesia`
`S$100 in baht through a Thai gateway` MEANS `rerouted purchase` (`purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Thai baht`) `A gateway in Thailand`
`S$100 in dong through a Vietnamese gateway` MEANS `rerouted purchase` (`purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Vietnamese dong`) `A gateway in Vietnam`
`S$4.99 local` MEANS `purchase for` `the base purchase` 4.99
`S$9.99 local` MEANS `purchase for` `the base purchase` 9.99
`S$7 local` MEANS `purchase for` `the base purchase` 7

-- cl.1(vii): UNI$3.5 per S$5 in Singapore: S$100 earns UNI$70 = 140 miles.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 local`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 70
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 local`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 70
#ASSERT fromMaybe 0 ((`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 local`)'s `miles certain`) EQUALS 140
-- cl.1(ix): charged in S$ overseas is not overseas.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in Singapore dollars overseas`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 70
-- cl.1(ix): UNI$6 per S$5 overseas: S$100 earns UNI$120 = 240 miles.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in US dollars through a gateway overseas`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT fromMaybe 0 ((`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in US dollars through a gateway overseas`)'s `miles certain`) EQUALS 240
-- cl.1(ix): an online foreign-currency charge with a Singapore gateway is local.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in US dollars through a Singapore gateway`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 70
-- ... and when she does not know the gateway: floor local, ceiling overseas.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in US dollars, gateway not known`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 70
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in US dollars, gateway not known`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT elem `The merchant's payment gateway is not known` ((`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in US dollars, gateway not known`)'s `depends on`)
-- cl.1(x): Regional UNI$7.5 per S$5: S$100 earns UNI$150 = 300 miles = 3 mpd.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in ringgit through a Malaysian gateway`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 150
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in rupiah through an Indonesian gateway`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 150
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in baht through a Thai gateway`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 150
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in dong through a Vietnamese gateway`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 150
#ASSERT fromMaybe 0 ((`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in ringgit through a Malaysian gateway`)'s `miles certain`) EQUALS 300
-- ... but only where the gateway is in the currency's own country.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in ringgit through a Thai gateway`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in ringgit through a Singapore gateway`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 70
-- ... and an unknown gateway: floor local 70, ceiling Regional 150.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in ringgit, gateway not known`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 70
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 in ringgit, gateway not known`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 150

-- cl.1(iv) and the per-five fork: S$4.99 earns nothing on blocks and 3 UNI$ pro rata (4.99 x 0.7 = 3.49);
-- S$9.99 earns 3 on blocks (1 x 3.5 = 3.5, down to 3) and 6 pro rata (6.99 down to 6);
-- S$7 earns 3 on blocks and 4 pro rata (4.9 down to 4).
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$4.99 local`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$4.99 local`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$9.99 local`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$9.99 local`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$7 local`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$7 local`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT elem `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)` ((`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$7 local`)'s `depends on`)
-- A multiple of S$5 is the same on both readings, and names no condition.
#ASSERT null ((`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 local`)'s `depends on`)

-- cl.1(ii): what earns nothing.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase of kind` `S$100 local` `Bill payment`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase of kind` `S$100 local` `Instalment plan charge`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase of kind` `S$100 local` `Cash advance`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase of kind` `S$100 local` `NETS or NETS-related transaction`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase of kind` `S$100 local` `SmartPay or personal loan`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase of kind` `S$100 local` `Top-up of a prepaid card or stored-value account`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase later reversed` `S$100 local`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`recoded purchase` `S$100 local` 7523))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`recoded purchase` `S$100 local` 6300))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`recoded purchase` `S$100 local` 9311))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`recoded purchase` `S$100 local` 8999))'s excluded
#ASSERT NOT ((`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`recoded purchase` `S$100 local` 5812))'s excluded)
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase described as` `S$100 local` `AXS`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase described as` `S$100 local` `Amaze`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase described as` `S$100 local` `EZ-Link`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase described as` `S$100 local` `SmoovPay`))'s excluded
#ASSERT NOT ((`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase described as` `S$100 local` `Youtrip`))'s excluded)
#ASSERT NOT ((`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase described as` `S$100 local` `ShopeePay`))'s excluded)

-- cl.1(ii)(d): Shell is excluded on every PRVI; SPC on all but the Amex.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase at merchant` `S$100 local` `Shell service station`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Amex` (`purchase at merchant` `S$100 local` `Shell service station`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase at merchant` `S$100 local` `SPC service station`))'s excluded
#ASSERT NOT ((`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Amex` (`purchase at merchant` `S$100 local` `SPC service station`))'s excluded)
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Amex` (`purchase at merchant` `S$100 local` `SPC service station`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 70

-- A bill paid directly on the card: the open reading.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase of kind` `S$100 local` `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase of kind` `S$100 local` `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`))'s `units at best` EQUALS 70

-- No category and no presentation: a wallet, a physical card and the web earn alike.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase paid by` `S$100 local` `Wallet tapped on a reader`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 70
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase paid by` `S$100 local` `Wallet used in an app or on a website`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 70
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase paid by` `S$100 local` `Card number entered online`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 70

-- SimplyGo (ABT): the local rate.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase of item` (`purchase at merchant` (`recoded purchase` `S$100 local` 4111) `SimplyGo`) `A SimplyGo bus or train fare`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 70

-- cl.2(i): Expedia, inside the booking period 1 April 2026 to 31 March 2027.
`S$100 at the Expedia PRVI site for a hotel on 5 October 2026` MEANS `purchase of item` (`purchase at merchant` `S$100 local` `Expedia PRVI site`) `An Expedia prepaid hotel booking`
`S$100 at the Expedia PRVI site for a flight on 5 October 2026` MEANS `purchase of item` (`purchase at merchant` `S$100 local` `Expedia PRVI site`) `An Expedia flight booking on a participating airline`
`S$100 at the Expedia PRVI site for a package on 5 October 2026` MEANS `purchase of item` (`purchase at merchant` `S$100 local` `Expedia PRVI site`) `An Expedia package booking`
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 at the Expedia PRVI site for a hotel on 5 October 2026`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 400
#ASSERT fromMaybe 0 ((`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 at the Expedia PRVI site for a hotel on 5 October 2026`)'s `miles certain`) EQUALS 800
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 at the Expedia PRVI site for a flight on 5 October 2026`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 150
-- ... a package is the open reading: floor the flight rate (150), ceiling the hotel rate (400).
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 at the Expedia PRVI site for a package on 5 October 2026`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 150
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 at the Expedia PRVI site for a package on 5 October 2026`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 400
-- ... outside the booking period the perk does not apply: 31 March 2027 is in, 1 April 2027 is out.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase posted on` (`purchase charged on` `S$100 at the Expedia PRVI site for a hotel on 5 October 2026` (Date 31 3 2027)) (Date 31 3 2027)))'s `units certain` EQUALS 400
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase posted on` (`purchase charged on` `S$100 at the Expedia PRVI site for a hotel on 5 October 2026` (Date 1 4 2027)) (Date 1 4 2027)))'s `units certain` EQUALS 70
-- ... and a booking paid at the hotel earns the ordinary rate.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase of item` `S$100 at the Expedia PRVI site for a hotel on 5 October 2026` `A hotel booking paid at the hotel`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 70

-- cl.2(ii): Agoda. Local UNI$17.5 per S$5 (S$100 -> 350 = 700 miles); other foreign currency UNI$20 (S$100 -> 400).
`S$100 at the Agoda PRVI site for a prepaid hotel` MEANS `purchase of item` (`purchase at merchant` `S$100 local` `Agoda PRVI site`) `An Agoda prepaid hotel booking`
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` `S$100 at the Agoda PRVI site for a prepaid hotel`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 350
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase in currency` `S$100 at the Agoda PRVI site for a prepaid hotel` `Another foreign currency`))'s `units at best` EQUALS 400
-- ... Japan accommodation is not a Qualifying Transaction.
#ASSERT (`UOB PRVI Miles earns on` `PRVI Visa` (`purchase of item` `S$100 at the Agoda PRVI site for a prepaid hotel` `An Agoda hotel booking in Japan`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 70

